  "summary": "To distinguish write refusals, check Redis INFO: if rdb_last_bgsave_status is err the writes are blocked due to snapshot (MISCONF) failure; if used_memory reaches maxmemory with a noeviction policy the writes are blocked because the store is full (OOM).",
  "likely_cause": "Not applicable – the answer describes how to determine the cause.",
  "confidence": "high",
